================================================================================================================
ENVELOPE DESCRIPTION -- target source 30m
================================================================================================================
  60,000 episodes, 5 features: vol_48, vratio, vol_slope, sandwich, off_mark
  target: running MAE and MFE, sign-folded, UNCLAMPED (see docstring)
  quantiles (0.05, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 0.95)   horizons ['0.5h', '1h', '2h', '5h', '10h']

======================================================================================================================
MATCHED 30-MINUTE vs 1-MINUTE TARGET -- same episodes, same split
======================================================================================================================
  THE QUESTION: the 30-minute target reads bar CLOSES, so it never sees the
  worst point inside a bar. Earlier work put the understatement near 0.3
  sigma, one-sided. Climatology is biased the same way, which is why the
  skill numbers were assumed largely unaffected. That was an ASSUMPTION.
  This stage tests it on the episodes where the minutes exist.

  HELD-OUT REUSE, STATED PLAINLY. These held-out episodes were already
  scored by the first envelope run. The halves analysis reused that run's
  cached predictions and refitted nothing; this stage fits new models and
  scores them on the same rows with a different target. That is the SECOND
  independent scoring of those episodes. It is a deliberate, named
  exception: there is no unscored block with 1-minute coverage, so the
  measurement question cannot be asked any other way. Confirmatory only.

[1m  ] 212 of 212 instruments have a 1-minute file
[1m  ] 131 begin at the backfill wall (2025-06-26/2025-06-27); 81 reach further back

  COVERAGE -- three rules, all measured. B is the one used.
  rule  episodes      fit  held out   pairs   days  span                      
  A        9,240    4,977     4,263     462    376  2025-07-11 .. 2026-10-04  
  B       53,757   35,693    18,064   3,000    466  2025-06-26 .. 2026-10-04  
  A = neither leg at the backfill wall. REPORTED, NOT USED: 46% of it is
      held out against 30% of the full set, and its 462 pairs are selected
      by which instruments got backfilled first.
  B = each leg's 1-minute history spans the window. USED. All 18,064
      held-out rows -- exactly the population run 1 scored -- so the
      30-minute arm sits on the same ground as the published numbers.
      B is a SPAN test, so its interior gaps were measured, not assumed:
      192 missing minutes of 32,307,957 (0.0006%), 7 episodes of 53,757
      affected, deepest 41. Trivial. Both structural checks pass on it.


  SELECTION, measured rather than asserted. Rule B's exclusion is purely
  TEMPORAL: it drops episodes entered before the backfill wall and keeps
  every pair, so the cross-section is intact (3,000 of 3,000) and the
  sample starts 2025-06-26 instead of 2024-09-18. That is a milder bias than
  A's: A is selected by which instruments were backfilled first, B by
  calendar alone.
  STILL NOT THE FULL 60,000. The fit block loses its first nine months, so
  nothing here describes the envelope over the whole history. It answers
  one question: on the episodes where the measurement can be checked, does
  the measurement fix matter.
