  THE TWO GAP COLUMNS ARE LEVELS and are a THIRD look at rows already
  scored twice -- confirmatory only. The 1m-30m COLUMN IS THE NEW
  MEASUREMENT: a within-row contrast on identical rows, split and day
  resamples, with only the target changing, so whatever the reuse did to
  the levels it did to both sides of the subtraction equally. Read the
  difference as the result of this stage and the levels as context.

======================================================================================================================
PINBALL SKILL vs CLIMATOLOGY -- within each target source
======================================================================================================================
  LEVELS, confirmatory only -- a third look at twice-scored rows.
  Each model against the climatology fitted on the SAME target source, so
  the two columns are each internally consistent. Positive = better than
  doing nothing. Comparing skill ACROSS sources is comparing two different
