======================================================================================================================
WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT SETTLE
======================================================================================================================
  Settles: on these 53,757 episodes, 3,000 pairs, whether the
  close-versus-true understatement changes the calibration gap. Same rows,
  same split, same models, same day resamples on both sides.
  The held-out arm is all 18,064 rows the first envelope run scored, so
  the 30-minute column is directly comparable to the published numbers.
  Does NOT settle: anything about the full 60,000. The fit block loses its
  first nine months to the backfill wall, so this describes the envelope over
  a shorter history. A null here is evidence the fix does not matter ON THESE
  ROWS, not that the understatement is small -- it is 0.46 to 0.68 sigma at
  10 hours, twice what this project assumed.
